WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.400 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  America fractured febrile furious old  wounds that have never healed pulled  apart in the middle of a pandemic a  country confronts the virus it's never  overcome racial division on the streets  of Minneapolis where George Floyd's  death lit this tinderbox  the protesters persisted undeterred by a  curfew with the police strikingly hard  to find the world is listening there are  opportunities for us to do that in a  constructive manner unfortunately there  are also those among us who would seek  to use this moment who would seek to use  his death as an excuse as a cover to  agitate for the destruction of those  same communities that have been most  traumatized by George Floyd's death but  in a society rich with inequity there is  anger at institutions  everywhere from Los Angeles to Colorado  and Kentucky  [Applause]  in Atlanta it was the CNN headquarters  targeted at the core of this although  unresolved rage at the disproportionate  number of African Americans killed by  police I'm mad as hell I woke up wanting  to see the world burn down yesterday  because I'm tired of seeing black in the  White House was also engulfed by  frustration the president warning  vicious dogs and ominous weapons would  have been deployed if protestors reached  the fence Derrick Chavan the officer who  put his knee on George Floyd's neck has  now been charged with third-degree  murder  but it's not enough for many this is a  nation in crisis rattled by dysfunction  smoldering with a leader currently  unable or unwilling to soothe Cordelia  Sky News Washington

